WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.953
An agent changed 39 files to move report exports to a background job. It sent this map of the change for review.

2
00:00:06.953 --> 00:00:13.147
Cards are parts of the system, grouped by layer and colour-coded by the type of change.

3
00:00:13.147 --> 00:00:21.453
A removed endpoint stands out. Select it to read the agent's summary, and comment on it.

4
00:00:21.453 --> 00:00:26.119
Select an interaction to open its code at the lines that implement it.

5
00:00:26.119 --> 00:00:30.927
Drag down the gutter to comment on a range of lines.

6
00:00:30.927 --> 00:00:37.730
Interface changes come with screenshots before and after. Comment on an area of either.

7
00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:45.099
When the order of calls matters, the agent adds a sequence diagram. Each message links to its code.

8
00:00:45.099 --> 00:00:52.833
A state diagram shows a lifecycle: here, a failed export stays running until its next attempt.

9
00:00:52.833 --> 00:01:01.266
Choose a file of the change, and the map lights up what touches it. Lines the map leaves out are marked.

10
00:01:01.266 --> 00:01:06.674
Mark each part as reviewed when you have read it. The header counts what is left.

11
00:01:06.674 --> 00:01:10.129
Then approve, or request changes.

12
00:01:10.129 --> 00:01:17.266
The agent gets back a structured decision: each comment tied to exactly what it is about.
